WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.690
Speaker 1: It was not just a speech in North
Carolina that former President Donald Trump

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.520
gave this weekend.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:12.140
Donald Trump, in his speech, made it clear
he's going to be the decider for Republicans

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.280
in twenty twenty two.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.160
He will say who is OK to reelect or to vote
for and who is not?

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.109
Who is a Republican in name only or someone
who has abandoned the party as far as Trump

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:24.640
is concerned.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.029
But Trump also recorded a Republican fundraising
video, and he is once again talking about

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.340
we're going to take back the White House sooner
than you think.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:41.780
Now, I know that in the absence of any other
data points, hearing Trump say we're going

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.350
to take back the White House sooner than you
think, it might not have any real meaning.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.449
That might not mean anything to us.

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:51.440
But when Trump says it, you have to understand
the context.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.690
Trump is suggesting he will be back in the
White House before January of twenty twenty

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.690
five.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:03.769
A normal person who hears a former president
say we will take back the White House.

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:09.370
That would mean to you at the next presidential
election, November of twenty twenty four.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:16.120
But the addition of sooner than you think
means exactly what Donald Trump has been telling

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.730
people, according to both Maggie Haberman
from The New York Times and the right wing

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:25.520
National Review, which is he is going to be
back in power sooner than when he could be

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.800
by winning in November of twenty twenty four.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.820
Here's the clip from this bizarre Trump fundraising
video.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.110
Speaker 2: I want to thank everybody for the
tremendous support you've shown.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.470
We're going to take back the Senate, take
back the House.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.140
We're going to take back the White House.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.110
And sooner than you think, it's going to be
really something special.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.590
Speaker 1: But we're going to take back the
White House sooner than you think.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:57.120
Trump is again, talking about somehow getting
Biden out before his term is up and getting

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.200
back in before Joe Biden's term is up.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:06.930
Now, I really hope that people understand,
even if for any reason Joe Biden did not complete

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:11.200
his term, Kamala Harris becomes the president,
not Donald Trump.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.400
They don't say, well, for some reason, Biden
is out.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.220
Let's go back to the last guy or the one before
that or the one before that.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.220
That's not how it works.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.470
It goes to the vice president.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:27.480
So aside from the ASP aspects of this that
relate to this being the same type of rhetoric,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.930
again, that eventually led to the January
six riots, will discuss that more probably

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.050
tomorrow.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:39.500
This is a complete fantasy world, understanding
or misunderstanding, better said of how our

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.960
government works.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.010
The video was posted to the YouTube channel
of the National Republican Senatorial Committee.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:54.560
The NRC, the Senate Republican fundraising
arm is what that is, and it was posted Friday.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.130
It's not exactly clear when it was recorded,
but it shows Trump floating similar ideas

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:04.170
to what he's reportedly been saying in private,
that somehow this guy is going to be reinstated

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.170
as president.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:10.890
Now, by itself, it might just sound like a
weirdly, weirdly phrased thing to say.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:17.240
But then The New York Times, The Washington
Post, the National Review are all reporting

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:23.540
that Donald Trump believes this bizarre election
audit or audits that are going on are somehow

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.390
going to put him back in power at some point.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.090
Isn't this seditious by Donald Trump?

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:34.600
Isn't this all pushing and pointing towards
rebellion against the established authority

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.970
of the United States, the current government?

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:41.870
Shouldn't someone go to the NSC or the North
Carolina Republican Party or whoever where

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:48.380
Trump has been saying this stuff and say what
exactly does sooner than you think mean?

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.640
Because that's really the question right now.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:56.360
What do you believe, sir, is the soonest possible
date at which Donald Trump could again be

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.430
president?

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:03.700
If the answer is anything other than January
of 20 25, when the next president is inaugurated,

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.700
then, you know, you're dealing with a wacky
person.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:12.270
And as these new Trump rallies start up again,
I would love to see this asked of the attendees.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.550
People that are there, what do you think is
the soonest that Donald Trump could again

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:19.509
be president and if they say anything other
than January of twenty, twenty five, it will

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:24.830
give you a real sense of where the electorate
is at this point in time.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.319
So a wacky, bizarre and deranged weekend.

